# Copy to `.env.local` (git-ignored) and fill in. Nothing here is committed with a value.

# The OpenRouter key used by the "Default" provider option in the app's settings.
#
# This is a SECRET and it is deliberately NOT `VITE_`-prefixed. Vite inlines every `VITE_*`
# variable into the bundle the browser downloads, which would publish the key to anyone who
# opens the page. This one is read only by the dev server's proxy (`vite.config.ts` →
# `src/lib/openrouter-proxy.ts`), which adds the `authorization` header server-side on requests
# to `/api/openrouter/*` and forwards them to https://openrouter.ai/api/v1.
#
# Consequence, stated plainly: the "Default" option works when the app is served by
# `bun run dev` (or by any host that proxies `/api/openrouter` and injects this header). Without
# the proxy the request reaches OpenRouter unauthenticated and OpenRouter's own 401 is shown.
#
# Get a key at https://openrouter.ai/keys
LARPABLE_OPENROUTER_DEFAULT_API_KEY=
